{
  "original_id": "primary-20260912-ray-west-j",
  "archive_id": "BW2-PR20260912-ray_west_j",
  "title": "A direct-sum law for the Ray–West correction and a statistic for separable permutations",
  "batch_label": "primary",
  "kind": "result-note",
  "original_status": "unresolved",
  "scope": "For every nonempty alpha in S_a and beta in S_b, let j(p)=(m^4+2m^3+m^2+4m+4)/2-g_2(p) for m=|p|, and let T(alpha), H(beta) indicate a decreasing last, respectively first, sum-indecomposable component, including singletons. Then j(alpha direct-sum beta)=j(alpha)+j(beta)+T(alpha)H(beta). Internal Ray--West good gaps restrict exactly to the summands and the join is good exactly when T(alpha)H(beta)=1. Value complementation gives the skew-sum rule with increasing skew components. Consequently j on every separable permutation equals the sum over maximal decomposition-tree nodes of adjacent decreasing-child pairs at sum nodes and adjacent increasing-child pairs at skew nodes. Among sum-decomposable permutations j(p)=|p|-1 if and only if p is layered; among skew-decomposable permutations equality holds if and only if p is colayered. No full-scope formula or equality classification is claimed for permutations indecomposable in both senses.",
  "gate_basis": "Current released terminal, manifest, PDF, TeX freeze, snapshot files, provenance and four audits agree.",
